{"result":"{
  "id": "18617",
  "key": "SFCC-317",
  "summary": "Zimmermann Benefits - PWA Kit Render",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want to build the Zimmermann Benefits PWA Kit render, so that the content authored in Contentful is displayed correctly, accessibly, and responsively within the cart drawer.\n\nThis story covers how the PWA Kit fetches and renders the Zimmermann Benefits content from Contentful (see SFCC-316](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-316)  for content authoring). This is not a component build — it is a render of Contentful-authored content fields. Each tile is built using the Contentful Icon and Text component [SFCC-835](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-835)  — containing an icon and text. The section renders a label and a set of benefit tiles. Background colour and styling are defined in the Zimmermann design system and are not content-authored.\n\nThe Zimmermann Benefits section appears in both the populated cart state (SFCC-825) and the empty cart state (SFCC-277). If the Contentful entry is unpublished or the fetch fails, the section does not render and the surrounding layout is unaffected.\n\nDesigns: [https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=40003224-108794&t=LoK8B0rP9ZfPNhuQ-0](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026) \n\nDesktop\n\n![\"image-20260817-031845.png\"](image-20260817-031845.png)\n\nMobile\n\n![\"image-20260828-002830.png\"](image-20260828-002830.png)",
